  "draftIsFinal": false,
  "summary": "I wrote the coin dash game in `src/main.ts`. It passes `typecheck`, but I haven't run `vite build` or the game in a browser, so the Aura3D rendering and the keyboard handling are untested.\n\n- **Scene:** `createAuraApp` draws into the existing `#app` canvas (resize off, pixel ratio 1). It shows a flat arena with walls and a blue sphere player. A fixed top-down perspective camera looks at the arena.\n- **Coins and movement:** Arrow keys and WASD move the player at constant speed, with diagonals normalised. There are 10 gold coins. Collecting one adds 1 to the score and respawns that coin using a seeded random generator (mulberry32). `R` resets the seed, so the same sequence repeats every round.\n- **Timestep and round:** The simulation runs at a fixed 1/60 s using an accumulator in my own `requestAnimationFrame` loop. The round is 1800 steps. The status becomes `won` as soon as the score reaches 15, and `lost` at 30 s otherwise.\n- **Pause and restart:** `P` freezes the simulation, and `R` restarts the round (score 0, timer 0, status `playing`). `P` does nothing once the round is won or lost.\n- **HUD:** A DOM bar under the canvas has elements with ids `score`, `time` (seconds remaining) and `status`.\n- **Eval hooks:** `window.__EVAL__.state()` returns `{ score, status, time }`, with time as elapsed simulated seconds. `step(n)` runs `n` fixed steps immediately using the current input state, and does nothing while paused or after the round has ended.\n- **Ready flag:** `window.__EVAL_READY__` is set on the first animation frame after `app.ready()` resolves. If the renderer takes longer than 5 s, it is set anyway.\n\nI used plain lights and a background colour instead of the Aura3D look presets, because the presets may try to load HDRI files that aren't available offline.\n\n",
